problem:
Problem description
- There is a retail staffing and sales planning problem with clerk categories indexed by $$i \in \mathcal{I}$$ over a monthly planning horizon $$\mathcal{T}$$.
- Each clerk category has a fixed headcount $$n_i$$, a standard monthly working time per clerk $$h_i$$, a sales productivity rate $$\alpha_i$$ measured in pairs per hour, a regular wage rate $$w_i$$, and an overtime wage rate $$\omega_i$$.
- Each sold pair yields unit profit $$\pi$$.
- The store pursues three ordered goals: achieve a target monthly sales volume $$D$$ for goal $$p_1$$, ensure full employment of all clerks for goal $$p_2$$, and minimize overtime usage for goal $$p_3$$.
- Required business rules:
  - The number of clerks in each category is fixed.
  - Regular working time available for each category is limited by the standard monthly hours for that category.
  - Any working time beyond the standard monthly hours is treated as overtime.
  - Sales volume is generated from worked hours using the category-specific productivity rate.
  - Overtime, if used, is compensated at the overtime wage rate of the corresponding category.
  - The sales target is a priority requirement, and any shortfall or excess relative to that target should be tracked.
  - Full employment means the plan should utilize the available standard monthly hours for the clerks before relying on overtime.
  - After higher-priority goals are addressed, overtime should be kept as small as possible.
  - Labor cost and sales profit may be reported as accounting outputs of the plan.
- A solution is represented by:
  - $$x_i$$: regular monthly hours assigned to clerk category $$i$$.
  - $$y_i$$: overtime monthly hours assigned to clerk category $$i$$.
  - $$s$$: total number of shoe pairs sold over $$\mathcal{T}$$.
  - $$d_g^-$$ and $$d_g^+$$: underachievement and overachievement deviations for each goal $$g \in \{1,2,3\}$$.
  - Optional reporting quantities such as total wage cost and total sales profit.

Input Format
{
  "clerk_categories": "list of clerk categories indexed by $$i \in \mathcal{I}$$",
  "headcount": {
    "shape": "$$|\\mathcal{I}|$$",
    "meaning": "fixed number of clerks $$n_i$$ in category $$i$$"
  },
  "standard_hours": {
    "shape": "$$|\\mathcal{I}|$$",
    "meaning": "standard monthly working hours per clerk $$h_i$$ in category $$i$$"
  },
  "productivity": {
    "shape": "$$|\\mathcal{I}|$$",
    "meaning": "sales productivity rate $$\\alpha_i$$ in pairs per hour for category $$i$$"
  },
  "regular_wage": {
    "shape": "$$|\\mathcal{I}|$$",
    "meaning": "regular wage rate $$w_i$$ per hour for category $$i$$"
  },
  "overtime_wage": {
    "shape": "$$|\\mathcal{I}|$$",
    "meaning": "overtime wage rate $$\\omega_i$$ per hour for category $$i$$"
  },
  "unit_profit": {
    "shape": "scalar",
    "meaning": "profit per sold pair $$\\pi$$"
  },
  "sales_target": {
    "shape": "scalar",
    "meaning": "target monthly sales volume $$D$$ for goal $$p_1$$"
  },
  "goal_priority": {
    "shape": "list of length $$3$$",
    "meaning": "priority order of goals $$p_1$$, $$p_2$$, and $$p_3$$"
  },
  "planning_horizon": {
    "shape": "set or scalar",
    "meaning": "monthly planning horizon $$\\mathcal{T}$$"
  }
}

Output Format
{
  "regular_hours": {
    "shape": "$$|\\mathcal{I}|$$ or $$|\\mathcal{I}| \\times |\\mathcal{T}|$$",
    "meaning": "planned regular hours $$x_i$$ or $$x_{i,t}$$"
  },
  "overtime_hours": {
    "shape": "$$|\\mathcal{I}|$$ or $$|\\mathcal{I}| \\times |\\mathcal{T}|$$",
    "meaning": "planned overtime hours $$y_i$$ or $$y_{i,t}$$"
  },
  "sales_volume": {
    "shape": "scalar or $$|\\mathcal{T}|$$",
    "meaning": "total pairs sold $$s$$ or period sales $$s_t$$"
  },
  "goal_deviations": {
    "under": {
      "shape": "$$3$$ or $$|\\mathcal{G}|$$",
      "meaning": "underachievement deviations $$d_g^-$$"
    },
    "over": {
      "shape": "$$3$$ or $$|\\mathcal{G}|$$",
      "meaning": "overachievement deviations $$d_g^+$$"
    }
  },
  "optional_reports": {
    "shape": "object",
    "meaning": "reported total labor cost and total sales profit"
  }
}

Example(s)

Input 1
{
  "clerk_categories": ["full_time", "part_time"],
  "headcount": [5, 4],
  "standard_hours": [160, 80],
  "productivity": [5, 2],
  "regular_wage": [1.0, 0.6],
  "overtime_wage": [1.5, 0.7],
  "unit_profit": 0.3,
  "sales_target": 5500,
  "goal_priority": ["p1", "p2", "p3"],
  "planning_horizon": "one_month"
}
